/-!
# Best-offender comparison and the line-normalizer field restriction

The maximum-elementary replacement `X C_U(X)` proves the full weight
comparison on the internal module U, and the actual Thompson action image
on U is generated by best offenders. The separately named source route now
uses `FullCoreTransfer.Source` to prove best generation of the SAME temporary
Thompson image on the first summand of U/E. It retains the odd action kernel,
then proves best generation on the whole faithful image for classification.
It does not use the old all-maximum-images-best or split-lift premises.

The actual quotient product `G/Q ≃ S₃ × image(C_G(E))`, with Q a normal
two-group, gives three-rank at most one for the centralizer factor. Given
the unreduced earlier classification and Borel-normalizer outputs, the
marked, orbit-generating first-summand geometry reduces the field
degrees to one and supplies genuine group equivalences with S₃, S₅ or
PSL₃(2). Its witness keeps the natural or doubled-natural central quotient,
the original central extension, the marker and the Sylow subgroup.

The source route supplies the full earlier classifier's generation hypothesis,
faithfulness, trivial two-core and genuine SQTK cover on the faithful image.
The marked subgroup is the literal image of J(S_E); its Sylow is the image of
the compatible intersection I ∩ q(S_E), and coprime normalizer lifting preserves
the original marker. All conditional earlier classification and exact Borel/
central-quotient witnesses remain explicit for the line-source parent to
discharge. No theorem here identifies the original I₀ or asserts index three.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), proof of
15.3.67, printed pp.1153–1154; B.1.2–3, p.68; B.4.2, p.86; B.5.1, p.99.
-/
